#ASSERT NOT (`s 295 I made and filed proof of my claim as the section requires` WITH `the creditor made proof of the claim under oath` IS TRUE, `the creditor caused the proof to be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE, `the proof was filed` IS TRUE, `the date the proof was filed` IS (YMD 2026 10 1), `the last day fixed for filing proofs of claim by the rules of the Court of Chancery or the order of the Court` IS (YMD 2026 9 30))
-- Not filed.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 295 I made and filed proof of my claim as the section requires` WITH `the creditor made proof of the claim under oath` IS TRUE, `the creditor caused the proof to be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE, `the proof was filed` IS FALSE, `the date the proof was filed` IS (YMD 2026 9 1), `the last day fixed for filing proofs of claim by the rules of the Court of Chancery or the order of the Court` IS (YMD 2026 9 30))
-- Not under oath.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 295 I made and filed proof of my claim as the section requires` WITH `the creditor made proof of the claim under oath` IS FALSE, `the creditor caused the proof to be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE, `the proof was filed` IS TRUE, `the date the proof was filed` IS (YMD 2026 9 1), `the last day fixed for filing proofs of claim by the rules of the Court of Chancery or the order of the Court` IS (YMD 2026 9 30))

-- s 295 I may be barred from the distribution of the assets
-- Proof filed in time: not barred.
#ASSERT (`s 295 I may be barred from the distribution of the assets` WITH `the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as section 295 requires` IS TRUE, `the Court of Chancery has directed that the creditor be barred from participating in the distribution` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No proof in time and the Court so directed: barred.
#ASSERT (`s 295 I may be barred from the distribution of the assets` WITH `the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as section 295 requires` IS FALSE, `the Court of Chancery has directed that the creditor be barred from participating in the distribution` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No proof in time, but the Court has not directed: 'may be barred' by direction of the Court, which the text leaves to the Court.
#ASSERT (`s 295 I may be barred from the distribution of the assets` WITH `the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as section 295 requires` IS FALSE, `the Court of Chancery has directed that the creditor be barred from participating in the distribution` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 295 the creditors have been given the notice the Court prescribed
-- The Court prescribed nothing: nothing is outstanding.
#ASSERT `s 295 the creditors have been given the notice the Court prescribed` WITH `the Court of Chancery has prescribed what notice, by publication or otherwise, is to be given to the creditors of the time fixed` IS FALSE, `the prescribed notice has been given to the creditors` IS FALSE
-- Prescribed and given.
#ASSERT `s 295 the creditors have been given the notice the Court prescribed` WITH `the Court of Chancery has prescribed what notice, by publication or otherwise, is to be given to the creditors of the time fixed` IS TRUE, `the prescribed notice has been given to the creditors` IS TRUE
-- Prescribed but not given.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 295 the creditors have been given the notice the Court prescribed` WITH `the Court of Chancery has prescribed what notice, by publication or otherwise, is to be given to the creditors of the time fixed` IS TRUE, `the prescribed notice has been given to the creditors` IS FALSE)

-- s 296(a) the trustee or receiver inspected the claims within 30 days after the notice
-- A creditor: inspected on the 30th day.
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the trustee or receiver inspected the claims within 30 days after the notice` WITH `the date the trustee or receiver received the Register's notice of the filing of the claims` IS (YMD 2026 6 1), `the date the trustee or receiver inspected the claims` IS (YMD 2026 7 1)
-- The 31st day.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(a) the trustee or receiver inspected the claims within 30 days after the notice` WITH `the date the trustee or receiver received the Register's notice of the filing of the claims` IS (YMD 2026 6 1), `the date the trustee or receiver inspected the claims` IS (YMD 2026 7 2))

-- s 296(a) the trustee or receiver must notify me that my claim is disputed
-- The receiver is not satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the trustee or receiver must notify me that my claim is disputed` WITH `the trustee or receiver is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS TRUE, `a creditor is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS FALSE
-- Another creditor is not satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the trustee or receiver must notify me that my claim is disputed` WITH `the trustee or receiver is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS FALSE, `a creditor is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS TRUE
-- Nobody disputes the claim.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(a) the trustee or receiver must notify me that my claim is disputed` WITH `the trustee or receiver is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS FALSE, `a creditor is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS FALSE)

-- s 296(a) I must submit to the examination on my disputed claim
-- Disputed and directed.
#ASSERT `s 296(a) I must submit to the examination on my disputed claim` WITH `the creditor’s claim is disputed` IS TRUE, `the trustee or receiver has directed an examination in relation to the claim` IS TRUE
-- No examination has been directed.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(a) I must submit to the examination on my disputed claim` WITH `the creditor’s claim is disputed` IS TRUE, `the trustee or receiver has directed an examination in relation to the claim` IS FALSE)
-- My claim is not disputed.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(a) I must submit to the examination on my disputed claim` WITH `the creditor’s claim is disputed` IS FALSE, `the trustee or receiver has directed an examination in relation to the claim` IS TRUE)

-- s 296(a) I must produce the books and papers the trustee or receiver requires on my disputed claim
-- Disputed and required.
#ASSERT `s 296(a) I must produce the books and papers the trustee or receiver requires on my disputed claim` WITH `the creditor’s claim is disputed` IS TRUE, `the trustee or receiver has required the production of books and papers relating to the claim` IS TRUE
-- Not disputed.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(a) I must produce the books and papers the trustee or receiver requires on my disputed claim` WITH `the creditor’s claim is disputed` IS FALSE, `the trustee or receiver has required the production of books and papers relating to the claim` IS TRUE)

-- s 296(a) the trustee or receiver has this power or duty on the claims
-- A creditor: the receiver may allow or disallow a claim, in whole or in part.
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the trustee or receiver has this power or duty on the claims` WITH `the power or duty` IS `to pass upon and allow or disallow the claims, or any part of them`
-- And must notify the claimants.
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the trustee or receiver has this power or duty on the claims` WITH `the power or duty` IS `to notify the claimants of the determination`

-- s 296(b) I may appeal the disallowance of my claim to the Court of Chancery
-- A creditor appeals on the 30th day.
#ASSERT `s 296(b) I may appeal the disallowance of my claim to the Court of Chancery` WITH `the creditor or claimant received notice from the receiver or trustee that the claim has been disallowed in whole or in part` IS TRUE, `the date the creditor or claimant received the notice` IS (YMD 2026 6 1), `the date the creditor or claimant appeals to the Court of Chancery` IS (YMD 2026 7 1)
-- On the 31st day: too late.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(b) I may appeal the disallowance of my claim to the Court of Chancery` WITH `the creditor or claimant received notice from the receiver or trustee that the claim has been disallowed in whole or in part` IS TRUE, `the date the creditor or claimant received the notice` IS (YMD 2026 6 1), `the date the creditor or claimant appeals to the Court of Chancery` IS (YMD 2026 7 2))
-- No notice of disallowance.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(b) I may appeal the disallowance of my claim to the Court of Chancery` WITH `the creditor or claimant received notice from the receiver or trustee that the claim has been disallowed in whole or in part` IS FALSE, `the date the creditor or claimant received the notice` IS (YMD 2026 6 1), `the date the creditor or claimant appeals to the Court of Chancery` IS (YMD 2026 6 5))

-- s 298 what is left for distribution after the receiver's compensation and costs
-- A stockholder: 1000 less 100, 50 and 25.
#ASSERT (`s 298 what is left for distribution after the receiver's compensation and costs` WITH `the assets of the corporation` IS 1000, `the compensation the Court of Chancery allows the receiver or trustee` IS 100, `the costs and expenses incurred in and about the execution of the trust` IS 50, `the costs of the proceedings in the Court` IS 25) EQUALS JUST 825
-- The assets do not cover the first payments: the section does not say what is left.
#ASSERT (`s 298 what is left for distribution after the receiver's compensation and costs` WITH `the assets of the corporation` IS 100, `the compensation the Court of Chancery allows the receiver or trustee` IS 100, `the costs and expenses incurred in and about the execution of the trust` IS 50, `the costs of the proceedings in the Court` IS 25) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 300 I have a lien for wages upon the assets of the insolvent corporation
-- An employee of an insolvent Delaware corporation.
#ASSERT `s 300 I have a lien for wages upon the assets of the insolvent corporation` WITH `the corporation is a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation doing business in this State` IS TRUE, `the corporation has become insolvent` IS TRUE, `the person does labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is an officer of the corporation` IS FALSE
-- An officer: the word 'employee' does not include any of the officers.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 300 I have a lien for wages upon the assets of the insolvent corporation` WITH `the corporation is a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation doing business in this State` IS TRUE, `the corporation has become insolvent` IS TRUE, `the person does labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is an officer of the corporation` IS TRUE)
-- The corporation has not become insolvent.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 300 I have a lien for wages upon the assets of the insolvent corporation` WITH `the corporation is a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation doing business in this State` IS TRUE, `the corporation has become insolvent` IS FALSE, `the person does labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is an officer of the corporation` IS FALSE)

-- s 300 the amount of my lien for wages
-- 5000 due, under the cap of 6000.
